Follow-up corrections for docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-09-review-correctif-fiabilisation-providers.md and the remaining T2/P2 items from the preceding review.

Scope and decisions:
- U1/U2: every LiteLLM refresh failure now emits the same structured event with a stable static reason, optional HTTP status, and an explicitly named entries_observed field. Network failure, rejected status, untrusted final redirect host, declared or streamed oversized body, stream failure, invalid UTF-8, parse rejection, cache-directory failure, and cache-write failure are observable. HTTP 304 remains an expected no-op.
- U3/U4: xAI catalog test imports are ordered normally and the older model-catalog identifier warning now uses the same structured logging style.
- V1: if the root provider catalog command fails while configured provider IDs remain available, each configured API provider receives a generic model_catalog_unavailable issue. The raw rejection never reaches the UI.
- V2: catalog issues obey the model-selector search by provider ID or display name.
- T2: OpenRouter routing observations now use their own bounded openrouter-routing.jsonl file. Successful routing evidence can no longer evict provider failures from provider-errors.jsonl.
- P2: malformed supported_parameters remains fail-closed for OpenRouter, which owns that metadata contract. Other OpenAI-compatible catalogs degrade the field to absent instead of hiding a usable model.
- Structural decision: catalog field validation moved to openai_compat_model_fields.rs after the parser crossed the 230-line project limit. Final production sizes are parser 188 lines and field validator 47 lines.
- V3 remains unchanged because the row is informational rather than actionable.

